1
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:19,150
A café sells one large pancake with a diameter of 30 centimetres for 8 dollars, or two small pancakes with diameters of 20 centimetres for 9 dollars.

2
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:24,220
Which gives more pancake: one 30 centimetre, or two 20 centimetre?

3
00:00:24,270 --> 00:00:27,690
Pause the video and choose.

4
00:00:27,740 --> 00:00:30,650
The one 30 centimetre pancake gives more.

5
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:34,150
Let's see why, with the area of a circle.

6
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:37,350
Remember: the diameter is twice the radius.

7
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:41,540
A diameter of 18 centimetres means a radius of 9.

8
00:00:41,590 --> 00:00:45,210
The circumference is pi times the diameter, or 2 pi R.

9
00:00:45,260 --> 00:00:48,070
Use the pi key on your calculator.

10
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:51,060
The area of a circle is pi R squared.

11
00:00:51,110 --> 00:00:51,730
Your turn.

12
00:00:51,780 --> 00:00:55,180
The area of a circle uses: pi R squared, or 2 pi R?

13
00:00:55,230 --> 00:00:58,410
Pause the video and choose.

14
00:00:58,460 --> 00:00:59,350
Pi R squared.

15
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:01,930
2 pi R is the circumference.

16
00:01:01,980 --> 00:01:04,420
The big pancake has radius 15.

17
00:01:04,470 --> 00:01:07,810
Its area is about 707 square centimetres.

18
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:13,740
Each small one has radius 10, so the two together have about 628.

19
00:01:13,790 --> 00:01:15,710
To work backwards, rearrange.

20
00:01:15,760 --> 00:01:18,690
From the area: R squared is A divided by pi.

21
00:01:18,740 --> 00:01:22,290
From the circumference: D is C divided by pi.

22
00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:24,740
For an exact answer, leave pi in.

23
00:01:24,790 --> 00:01:28,040
A radius of 7 gives an area of 49 pi.

24
00:01:28,090 --> 00:01:29,380
Here is the method.

25
00:01:29,430 --> 00:01:32,480
Step 1: find the radius or diameter.

26
00:01:32,530 --> 00:01:36,700
Step 2: choose the formula: circumference or area.

27
00:01:36,750 --> 00:01:40,750
Step 3: work it out with the pi key, or leave pi in.

28
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:43,720
Step 4: round, and give the units.

29
00:01:43,770 --> 00:01:47,420
A bike wheel has a diameter of 64 centimetres.

30
00:01:47,470 --> 00:01:53,500
In one turn it travels pi times 64, which is about 201.1 centimetres.

31
00:01:53,550 --> 00:01:57,210
A round rug has an area of 2.5 square metres.

32
00:01:57,260 --> 00:02:00,840
R squared is 2.5 divided by pi, about 0.796.

33
00:02:00,890 --> 00:02:03,540
So R is about 0.89 metres.

34
00:02:03,590 --> 00:02:04,220
Your turn.

35
00:02:04,270 --> 00:02:05,740
A circle has radius 5.

36
00:02:05,790 --> 00:02:08,010
What is its area, in terms of pi?

37
00:02:08,060 --> 00:02:10,920
Pause and work it out.

38
00:02:10,970 --> 00:02:14,920
5 squared is 25, so the area is 25 pi.

39
00:02:14,970 --> 00:02:20,900
A semicircle with diameter 10: the curve is half of 10 pi, about 15.7.

40
00:02:20,950 --> 00:02:23,120
Add the straight edge, 10.

41
00:02:23,170 --> 00:02:27,090
The perimeter is about 25.7 centimetres.

42
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:29,680
A circle has diameter 8 centimetres.

43
00:02:29,730 --> 00:02:31,050
Kai finds the area.

44
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:33,040
Which line is wrong?

45
00:02:33,090 --> 00:02:34,200
Line 1 is wrong.

46
00:02:34,250 --> 00:02:38,030
The area formula uses the radius, which is 4.

47
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:43,760
Pi times 4 squared is 16 pi, about 50.3 square centimetres.

48
00:02:43,810 --> 00:02:47,440
A bike computer counts how many times the wheel turns.

49
00:02:47,490 --> 00:02:52,840
It multiplies by the circumference to work out how far you have ridden.

50
00:02:52,890 --> 00:02:54,130
One last question.

51
00:02:54,180 --> 00:02:59,100
Find the circumference of a circle with radius 3, to 1 decimal place.

52
00:02:59,150 --> 00:03:02,450
Pause the video and answer.

53
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:07,250
2 times pi times 3 is 6 pi, which is about 18.8.

54
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:11,280
To remember: the circumference is pi D, or 2 pi R.

55
00:03:11,330 --> 00:03:12,930
The area is pi R squared.

56
00:03:12,980 --> 00:03:14,470
Use the radius.

57
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:17,090
Rearrange to work backwards.

58
00:03:17,140 --> 00:03:19,700
For exact answers, leave pi in.

59
00:03:19,750 --> 00:03:24,950
Great work! Now practise lesson 7.1 on Camday.
